Don't say like that.

259
00:20:46,626 --> 00:20:48,181
Even if you say that, a mother’s a mother, you know

260
00:20:48,286 --> 00:20:51,707
I told you from the start that something like this would never end well

261
00:20:52,453 --> 00:20:54,212
You threw her out of the house

262
00:20:54,950 --> 00:20:58,148
Not all factory workers are like that.

263
00:20:58,173 --> 00:21:00,714
That's why you're a doting parent.

264
00:21:01,430 --> 00:21:03,686
Thinking that only your own daughter is smart...

265
00:21:03,710 --> 00:21:06,196
Since you swagger around

266
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,106
this is what happens

267
00:21:08,130 --> 00:21:10,337
It’s because Mom’s kind of sloppy,

268
00:21:11,367 --> 00:21:13,728
She come back and
messing things up like this, you know—

269
00:21:14,432 --> 00:21:15,349
I’m back.

270
00:21:20,085 --> 00:21:22,144
I just made sure the place was shut up pretty tight, okay?

271
00:21:23,903 --> 00:21:24,707
Oh, should I help?

272
00:21:25,111 --> 00:21:27,283
You said you’ll take a bath first.

273
00:21:29,804 --> 00:21:31,191
Sister takes the bath too,right?

274
00:21:31,329 --> 00:21:35,481
She can't take the bath.
She have to clean the room.

275
00:21:39,390 --> 00:21:43,195
Where are you going, huh?

276
00:21:45,309 --> 00:21:46,063
Sis.

277
00:21:47,101 --> 00:21:47,588
Ino

278
00:21:48,053 --> 00:21:49,304
you said too much.

279
00:21:49,354 --> 00:21:50,747
You have no right to speak ill of others.

280
00:21:50,952 --> 00:21:51,936
What's the hell?

281
00:21:52,872 --> 00:21:56,836
You gave birth to a foolish daughter.

282
00:21:57,046 --> 00:21:59,782
You’re the one who keeps being moody and either going to work or not going

283
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,950
Whenever you visit your parents, all you do is complain.

284
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:06,760
There are times when it's okay to get angry, and times when it's not

285
00:22:07,350 --> 00:22:09,036
You should let your dad get angry

286
00:22:09,208 --> 00:22:11,354
You don't get to butt in like you're so great

287
00:22:11,687 --> 00:22:13,822
Even your dad is going to stop talking and just keep quiet now, so

288
00:22:14,930 --> 00:22:19,566
Don’t you think we all should just be quiet and keep things calm from now on?

289
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:28,120
I'll cook soon so take a bath first.

290
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:31,480
Where's my shoes?

291
00:22:31,855 --> 00:22:33,268
I'll wash your back?

292
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,640
I left them here

293
00:22:35,739 --> 00:22:37,265
Why don’t we get in together?

294
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:39,446
Before long there’ll be food ready,

295
00:22:39,471 --> 00:22:40,357
Sis.

296
00:22:40,828 --> 00:22:42,107
so stop bothering me.

297
00:22:42,756 --> 00:22:44,926
What’s with you acting so arrogant and sulking?

298
00:22:45,178 --> 00:22:47,118
You’re the one who’s behaving all high and mighty

299
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:50,985
They send me gifts on Mother's Day.

300
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,096
but all you do is come here to get money.

301
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,692
Whenever you show up, it’s nothing but trouble

302
00:22:55,717 --> 00:22:56,332
Bros

303
00:22:56,726 --> 00:22:59,000
it’s been a long time since she came back, and you shouldn’t be saying things like that to your sister.

304
00:22:59,120 --> 00:22:59,993
What?

305
00:23:00,670 --> 00:23:02,303
Just get out.

306
00:23:03,972 --> 00:23:08,160
If I’m here, I'm causing trouble for everyone

307
00:23:08,313 --> 00:23:10,695
Oh, yeah—that’s for your sake,

308
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:13,356
Your sister couldn’t manage a proper marriage into a good home anymore

309
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:20,570
Bro, My sis have been working in the factory
for six years just to get me to school

310
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:23,689
I can’t help thinking, how am I supposed to repay her for that?

311
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:28,369
I want to get my certification quickly so I can let my older sister take it easy.

312
00:23:30,369 --> 00:23:31,252
San-chan....

313
00:23:34,153 --> 00:23:37,814
I was planning to go out once the sun went down

314
00:23:40,799 --> 00:23:42,205
Sis...

315
00:23:42,705 --> 00:23:45,447
so what are you planning to do about it?

316
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:48,586
I'll ask my friend who works at the hospital

317
00:23:48,610 --> 00:23:50,799
It’s not like it’s already too late

318
00:23:51,838 --> 00:23:52,791
There are other methods as well.

319
00:24:00,211 --> 00:24:01,477
Brother

320
00:24:03,061 --> 00:24:06,627
You know, right after you got out of junior high,

321
00:24:07,030 --> 00:24:09,166
didn’t you lure a girl into the back area and get caught by Dad?

322
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:13,300
Back then, I was the one who protected you, you know

323
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:16,392
Tell him she’s a girl from your classmate.

324
00:24:16,836 --> 00:24:18,916
And then, brother—

325
00:24:19,310 --> 00:24:22,310
You were thanking (me) by doing the hand-over-hand gesture in a dark place, weren’t you?

326
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:25,119
It's just that...

327
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:27,956
Why do you treat me like that?

328
00:24:27,995 --> 00:24:30,995
I am very sad that you said that to me.

329
00:24:31,020 --> 00:24:32,266
I will try asking someone else.

330
00:24:32,291 --> 00:24:33,265
It's not good.

331
00:24:33,973 --> 00:24:37,249
The name "Mon" means "the gate of excruciating agony."

332
00:24:37,443 --> 00:24:39,319
It’s named because you pass out when you leave—the name says so

333
00:24:39,430 --> 00:24:41,806
My sister’s name San is the name of the terrible—like, it’s basically the one from the worst

334
00:24:41,830 --> 00:24:43,586
"Ino," part of my name, means "pig."

335
00:24:44,076 --> 00:24:47,076
Our father is the kind of fool who would give us a name like this.

336
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:48,765
I can’t just keep quiet

337
00:24:49,150 --> 00:24:51,195
You say, 'Settle this quickly,'
What do you mean?

338
00:24:51,391 --> 00:24:55,891
I will raise my own child myself.

339
00:24:57,679 --> 00:25:01,483
This feeling—it's something you just can't understand

340
00:25:02,281 --> 00:25:04,195
You are a truly terrible person.

341
00:25:04,577 --> 00:25:08,022
I am not going to worry you anymore

342
00:25:09,083 --> 00:25:10,250
Alright then,

343
00:25:10,275 --> 00:25:11,149
Sis...

344
00:25:12,187 --> 00:25:13,984
Just wait

345
00:25:15,547 --> 00:25:16,797
Mon

346
00:25:17,242 --> 00:25:18,289
Sis.

347
00:25:21,742 --> 00:25:22,492
Ino.

348
00:25:23,541 --> 00:25:25,781
Watch on the bath.
Fire is dangerous.

349
00:25:36,969 --> 00:25:38,211
Sis.

350
00:25:42,438 --> 00:25:43,305
Sis.

351
00:25:44,396 --> 00:25:45,898
Sis! Wait!

352
00:25:52,274 --> 00:25:53,977
Sis! Wait!

353
00:25:55,180 --> 00:25:56,625
Sis!

354
00:26:01,539 --> 00:26:04,539
Sis! Come back home!

355
00:26:04,860 --> 00:26:06,875
You should go back home.

356
00:26:07,391 --> 00:26:08,195
Mon.

357
00:26:10,094 --> 00:26:11,242
Hold on.

358
00:26:15,389 --> 00:26:17,320
Mother! Are you alright?

359
00:27:11,992 --> 00:27:12,508
Hey.

360
00:27:15,521 --> 00:27:17,047
Please take this.

361
00:27:22,338 --> 00:27:24,507
Thank you for coming all the way.

362
00:27:25,125 --> 00:27:27,258
I just came to say hello.

363
00:27:40,539 --> 00:27:42,117
You bastard!

364
00:27:42,844 --> 00:27:44,320
You damn fool!

365
00:27:50,328 --> 00:27:51,145
Don't make a fool of us.

366
00:27:54,038 --> 00:27:55,054
Don't be too violent with her.

367
00:27:56,013 --> 00:27:58,757
Because she’s Rosa’s maid, I’m letting it
slide and giving her a bit of extra leeway

368
00:27:59,032 --> 00:28:01,179
She asked us to pay for the cream,

369
00:28:01,407 --> 00:28:02,183
so I got mad

370
00:28:02,781 --> 00:28:05,264
I am really frustrated.

371
00:28:08,289 --> 00:28:09,375
It can't be helped.

372
00:28:13,251 --> 00:28:15,914
Remember.

373
00:28:16,336 --> 00:28:17,750
You get it?

374
00:28:19,539 --> 00:28:20,843
You bastard!

375
00:28:22,625 --> 00:28:23,950
Just calm down already!

376
00:28:24,359 --> 00:28:26,406
Everyone says, 'This is a temple of art,

377
00:28:26,431 --> 00:28:28,226
Your presence is an eyesore.

378
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:57,184
I told her, though

379
00:28:57,641 --> 00:29:00,387
She shouldn't take money by force the people at the cabaret

380
00:29:00,521 --> 00:29:04,047
But, like,She came yesterday, too.

381
00:29:04,220 --> 00:29:06,406
Just a little bit of money

382
00:29:06,431 --> 00:29:07,602
Who do we owe that to?

383
00:29:07,875 --> 00:29:08,786
Sorry to trouble you

384
00:29:08,810 --> 00:29:09,859
I’ll make sure to tell her.

385
00:29:10,220 --> 00:29:11,382
so—go call Mon-chan

386
00:29:11,484 --> 00:29:12,706
I’ll get her to apologize properly

387
00:29:13,750 --> 00:29:14,516
Have a seat, boss.

388
00:29:15,264 --> 00:29:17,663
But I am not really a boss yet

389
00:29:17,727 --> 00:29:19,000
Come on.

390
00:29:19,528 --> 00:29:21,354
Excuse me.

391
00:29:27,242 --> 00:29:28,117
I’m sorry.

392
00:29:29,859 --> 00:29:31,615
Even if she know a man like that—

393
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:34,649
She can’t expect it to be an appeal for the stage, right?

394
00:29:35,647 --> 00:29:38,109
Well, I guess she’s a junior from the factory

395
00:29:38,217 --> 00:29:40,013
Everyone is cold to her.

396
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:43,552
In the end, she came to rely on me, so…

397
00:29:43,912 --> 00:29:46,920
She probably don’t plan to become a nude dancer, though

398
00:29:47,746 --> 00:29:49,057
If it pays well,

399
00:29:49,090 --> 00:29:50,990
She might change her mind again

400
00:29:51,604 --> 00:29:53,302
Oh she's here

401
00:29:53,826 --> 00:29:54,982
Come in.

402
00:29:58,255 --> 00:29:59,041
Mom-chan

403
00:29:59,255 --> 00:30:01,308
Are you planning to take the stage

404
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:02,146
She can’t

405
00:30:02,935 --> 00:30:03,535
It's impossible.

406
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:04,599
That would be… not now

407
00:30:04,830 --> 00:30:05,693
Oh, I see

408
00:30:07,901 --> 00:30:11,955
I know someone in Hanamaki

409
00:30:12,455 --> 00:30:13,758
Leave her over there

410
00:30:14,728 --> 00:30:15,880
At hot-spring resort?

411
00:30:17,326 --> 00:30:18,263
Where?

412
00:30:19,021 --> 00:30:20,013
It’s Tohoku

413
00:30:21,368 --> 00:30:25,505
Just go there to recuperate, and once you’ve figured things out,

414
00:30:26,002 --> 00:30:27,880
you can have it handled by paying back your obligations

415
00:30:31,099 --> 00:30:34,294
You should become a dancer., you know

416
00:30:39,443 --> 00:30:40,626
Until I give a birth

417
00:30:41,505 --> 00:30:44,500
I’ll put up with anything

418
00:30:46,612 --> 00:30:50,232
Please let me stay by your side.

419
00:30:50,873 --> 00:30:51,592
Yeah

420
00:30:51,910 --> 00:30:54,419
You are also very much into going to places you don't know.

421
00:30:55,250 --> 00:30:58,232
She was very cute when she worked at the factory.

422
00:30:58,390 --> 00:31:01,927
We’ve been encouraging each other through the tough times

423
00:31:02,465 --> 00:31:04,644
She quit the factory because she was head over heels for him.

424
00:31:04,732 --> 00:31:05,560
Why are you saying that now?

425
00:31:05,724 --> 00:31:10,763
I ended up putting the company and the trumpet-maker Takeru on the back burner,

426
00:31:10,820 --> 00:31:11,836
so it’s a loss, really

427
00:31:11,860 --> 00:31:12,496
Even if you say that…

428
00:31:12,520 --> 00:31:14,458
His asthma was unexpected.

429
00:31:14,937 --> 00:31:18,911
Why are you acting like you don’t even know the inside story, too?

430
00:31:19,325 --> 00:31:21,021
I am not the boss.

431
00:31:21,630 --> 00:31:24,386
Well, think about it, Mon-chan

432
00:31:24,410 --> 00:31:27,410
He tries to help you.

433
00:31:30,217 --> 00:31:33,865
You'll only be in the way if you stay here.

434
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:36,599
Yeah.

435
00:33:20,164 --> 00:33:23,164
This person? she's not here

436
00:33:26,180 --> 00:33:27,458
Do you happen to have any idea?

437
00:33:28,130 --> 00:33:30,185
Why don’t you apply to be a missing-person caller on TV?

438
00:33:31,609 --> 00:33:32,536
See you again!

439
00:33:32,561 --> 00:33:33,482
Thanks.

440
00:34:48,623 --> 00:34:49,740
You came back late.

441
00:34:51,536 --> 00:34:52,591
Couldn't you find her?

442
00:34:54,825 --> 00:34:56,021
I hope you’ll know

443
00:34:57,430 --> 00:34:58,796
Cheer up!

444
00:34:58,821 --> 00:35:00,911
You’ve got to sleep—you’re up early tomorrow morning

445
00:35:28,279 --> 00:35:29,763
In a year

446
00:35:32,802 --> 00:35:35,044
Next is Yazaki, Yazaki.

447
00:35:35,248 --> 00:35:38,006
Please press the buzzer if you are getting off.

448
00:35:59,215 --> 00:36:00,779
Thank you very much

449
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:05,083
Thank you in advance.
We appreciate your cooperation

450
00:36:05,159 --> 00:36:07,425
Likewise—thank you very much.
I look forward to working with you

451
00:36:09,505 --> 00:36:14,136
Thanks so much for taking the time despite how busy you are—thank you

452
00:36:26,466 --> 00:36:27,372
Hello?

453
00:36:28,087 --> 00:36:31,044
You look like a completely different person.

454
00:36:33,381 --> 00:36:34,826
How are sales of amazake?

455
00:36:35,057 --> 00:36:37,599
No—it's the age of canned juice

456
00:36:38,070 --> 00:36:39,776
Well, even though it was this busy schedule...

457
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:42,800
Just look—No one rents our boat.

458
00:36:44,260 --> 00:36:46,849
Please try this amazake.

459
00:36:48,482 --> 00:36:49,967
Did you hear anything from my older sister?

460
00:36:51,982 --> 00:36:53,107
No?

461
00:36:54,849 --> 00:36:56,325
Excuse me.

462
00:36:57,443 --> 00:36:59,201
Welcome.

463
00:36:59,856 --> 00:37:05,004
I heard about this from Akaza-san below.

464
00:37:05,151 --> 00:37:07,552
Akaza’s shop is right here, but…

465
00:37:11,865 --> 00:37:13,974
Well, I am Obata

466
00:37:16,044 --> 00:37:17,896
Is Monko here?

467
00:37:19,854 --> 00:37:20,927
What do you need?

468
00:37:22,029 --> 00:37:23,732
She is in Tokyo right now

469
00:37:26,591 --> 00:37:31,091
but actually, I want to talk about Monko

470
00:37:32,540 --> 00:37:34,536
So I came, but...

471
00:37:35,430 --> 00:37:39,872
Well, I’m sorry, but could you go over to our side?

472
00:37:42,590 --> 00:37:45,638
Take him along and I'll go call your father

473
00:37:49,834 --> 00:37:50,451
Come with me.

474
00:38:00,724 --> 00:38:03,771
Yeah, Ken-chan, Ken-chan—could you do me a favor?
Please look after the shop.

475
00:38:03,849 --> 00:38:05,255
I’ll give you some extra money later,

476
00:38:05,507 --> 00:38:06,747
just for a little while—okay?

477
00:38:06,803 --> 00:38:07,654
Sure.

478
00:38:07,712 --> 00:38:08,794
Thank you very much.

479
00:38:59,398 --> 00:39:00,413
Please wait a moment.

480
00:39:19,882 --> 00:39:21,304
Father

481
00:39:23,828 --> 00:39:25,187
Father

482
00:39:27,054 --> 00:39:28,304
Hurry up

483
00:39:29,753 --> 00:39:33,628
Mon's guy.....

484
00:39:34,542 --> 00:39:36,705
That person, a student, has arrived

485
00:39:37,003 --> 00:39:38,018
Mon's?

486
00:39:39,858 --> 00:39:41,916
Boss, I’ll bring the rope nets.

487
00:39:43,406 --> 00:39:44,627
Sorry.

488
00:39:50,575 --> 00:39:52,401
Please don’t do anything rough, okay?

489
00:39:52,829 --> 00:39:55,072
Because the other person is young student

490
00:39:55,277 --> 00:39:58,893
I guess he probably came to take care of regarding the baby

491
00:40:07,397 --> 00:40:10,855
Dad, please—I’m begging you, don’t be rough, okay?

492
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:12,138
Does he have a bad appearance?

493
00:40:12,239 --> 00:40:14,057
He looks like a very good student.

494
00:40:43,796 --> 00:40:45,315
Please come in

495
00:40:51,977 --> 00:40:53,565
Stay at the shop.

496
00:40:56,250 --> 00:40:58,440
Please come in

497
00:41:05,604 --> 00:41:06,362
Please come in

498
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:29,697
You can’t talk over there

499
00:41:33,168 --> 00:41:36,666
Please feel free to come in.

500
00:41:36,818 --> 00:41:37,916
So, please come here

501
00:41:40,026 --> 00:41:41,362
Excuse me.

502
00:41:50,855 --> 00:41:53,855
Let's have you state the request quickly.

503
00:41:57,354 --> 00:41:59,333
I haven’t even greeted you yet

504
00:42:01,057 --> 00:42:02,799
I am Obata

505
00:42:03,924 --> 00:42:06,934
It is not as if I have been ignoring the problem until now.

506
00:42:07,540 --> 00:42:11,401
I was being watched by the country's father so I didn’t have any chance to slip away

507
00:42:14,831 --> 00:42:16,327
I’m really sorry.
I ended up causing such an inconvenience.

508
00:42:20,974 --> 00:42:23,974
Actually, I’m going to Tokyo next time—

509
00:42:24,914 --> 00:42:34,299
I’d like to cover various costs and, as a way of making up for it, to repay my parents in my own way

510
00:42:35,953 --> 00:42:36,783
So,

511
00:42:40,108 --> 00:42:47,447
I want to have an abortion for the sake of us both....

512
00:42:49,780 --> 00:42:53,114
It may be presumptuous, but I tried to be as mindful of that point as I could

513
00:42:56,540 --> 00:42:59,540
But then— you know?

514
00:43:00,930 --> 00:43:04,153
Did she have a successful abortion?

515
00:43:10,820 --> 00:43:14,192
Did you come because you wanted to feel at ease yourself?

516
00:43:15,950 --> 00:43:17,122
No, I mean—

517
00:43:17,348 --> 00:43:21,083
You just thought you could get things
sorted out for yourself and came here,or what?

518
00:43:21,565 --> 00:43:22,690
Don't get me wrong.

519
00:43:23,839 --> 00:43:24,766
I just want to make amends.

520
00:43:24,791 --> 00:43:28,033
And you think we can make up for it
by paying the cost of taking care of the abortion?

521
00:43:28,270 --> 00:43:30,976
No—if it’s at all something I can do...

522
00:43:33,007 --> 00:43:34,299
Um… with all my sincerity.

523
00:43:35,862 --> 00:43:37,378
She miscarried the baby

524
00:43:41,534 --> 00:43:44,323
She has been out of her mind ever since.

525
00:43:54,463 --> 00:43:55,375
So she is...

526
00:43:55,408 --> 00:43:56,963
Mon

527
00:43:58,222 --> 00:43:59,842
Where is she now?

528
00:44:00,944 --> 00:44:03,143
If you don’t mind, could you tell me her address?

529
00:44:04,881 --> 00:44:06,721
I want to meet her once and apologize

530
00:44:08,216 --> 00:44:12,088
I need to clear things up emotionally—otherwise,

531
00:44:13,100 --> 00:44:14,237
it’s just not going to work out, you know

532
00:44:15,292 --> 00:44:16,081
Well...

533
00:44:16,690 --> 00:44:18,586
I got her back for the moment,

534
00:44:18,610 --> 00:44:21,760
but She left without saying where she was going.

535
00:44:27,205 --> 00:44:27,847
Old lady

536
00:44:28,283 --> 00:44:30,955
So, the store’s manju—
Older sister wants to give this to you.

537
00:44:30,980 --> 00:44:31,936
San chan?

538
00:44:32,381 --> 00:44:34,697
she said you should let the customers have it to eat

539
00:44:34,722 --> 00:44:36,487
Ha ha, thanks for your hard work

540
00:44:47,666 --> 00:44:51,510
Please have this steamed bun if you'd like.

541
00:44:53,386 --> 00:44:54,331
Please.

542
00:45:01,283 --> 00:45:05,533
She doesn't want to talk to you.

543
00:45:06,135 --> 00:45:08,080
You should go home.

544
00:45:16,691 --> 00:45:20,940
Mr. Obata, you'd better stop making crimes like this

545
00:45:21,580 --> 00:45:23,737
This time, you were the one who won

546
00:45:57,018 --> 00:45:59,240
He’s always the kind of person who is like that, you see

547
00:45:59,706 --> 00:46:01,112
He’s not very good with words.

548
00:46:03,047 --> 00:46:05,354
I'd like to have you come up for dinner,

549
00:46:09,283 --> 00:46:15,362
but then, Mom, I’m afraid I've really inconvenienced you

550
00:46:16,335 --> 00:46:19,335
Then, if—as it happens—Mon returns home…

551
00:46:20,222 --> 00:46:23,010
I’ll say that you came to visit.

552
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:29,080
But once you find out her address, please ask about it

553
00:46:36,459 --> 00:46:38,971
This is something small.

554
00:46:39,128 --> 00:46:40,190
What's this?

555
00:46:40,479 --> 00:46:43,135
Well, it’s a little embarrassing, but…

556
00:46:43,250 --> 00:46:44,987
You don't need to do that.

557
00:46:45,012 --> 00:46:45,870
Please take it.

558
00:46:46,660 --> 00:46:48,173
I was hoping you wouldn’t have to worry like that

559
00:46:48,307 --> 00:46:52,385
I thought I could have bought something as a souvenir, but

560
00:46:55,150 --> 00:46:56,705
Please accept this at least.

561
00:46:56,776 --> 00:46:57,518
If you don’t…

562
00:47:00,963 --> 00:47:11,846
I probably won’t be of any help, but please, at least
take my feelings into consideration—please accept this

563
00:47:12,860 --> 00:47:14,635
Please don’t just reject it and send it back

564
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:15,994
Please

565
00:47:20,580 --> 00:47:22,494
Well then, I’ll take my leave with that

566
00:47:23,009 --> 00:47:30,537
Please take care , and let your husband know
that I hope he won’t take it the wrong way

567
00:47:32,346 --> 00:47:33,401
Excuse me.

568
00:47:45,033 --> 00:47:46,969
So this is Ayame?

569
00:47:47,494 --> 00:47:48,041
Yes

570
00:47:50,907 --> 00:47:52,486
And what about this one?

571
00:47:52,627 --> 00:47:53,877
Summer Chrysanthemums.

572
00:47:54,510 --> 00:47:56,900
In summer, this must be beautiful, doesn’t it?

573
00:47:57,610 --> 00:48:00,610
What color is the Summer Chrysanthemums?

574
00:48:01,800 --> 00:48:02,978
It's a yellow flower

575
00:48:17,611 --> 00:48:19,691
How old are you?

576
00:48:20,361 --> 00:48:20,986
Me?

577
00:48:21,931 --> 00:48:23,853
I just turned twenty-four

578
00:48:24,249 --> 00:48:26,725
Oh, then just one year apart from Mon

579
00:48:26,820 --> 00:48:27,415
Yes

580
00:48:50,297 --> 00:48:52,001
This is my address, but—

581
00:48:52,559 --> 00:48:54,325
Could you please give this to Mon?

582
00:48:54,350 --> 00:48:56,439
Yes, I’m sure I will

583
00:48:57,152 --> 00:48:59,658
Apparently, she also changes their mood from time to time

584
00:48:59,690 --> 00:49:02,690
She sometimes comes over without even letting me know.

585
00:49:03,530 --> 00:49:07,415
If you happen to meet her....

586
00:49:08,235 --> 00:49:09,885
well—I'll tell her

587
00:49:09,925 --> 00:49:12,626
Here—please have some

588
00:49:14,767 --> 00:49:16,910
Well then, goodbye.

589
00:49:26,855 --> 00:49:27,527
See you.

590
00:51:27,992 --> 00:51:29,628
Hey, wait a minute!

591
00:51:37,299 --> 00:51:38,449
I'm Mon's brother.

592
00:51:41,577 --> 00:51:42,980
I have something to tell you.

593
00:51:45,960 --> 00:51:47,769
Go down that far.

594
00:52:04,202 --> 00:52:05,838
Did you meet Mon afterward?

595
00:52:07,840 --> 00:52:08,574
Yes, I didn't

596
00:52:11,496 --> 00:52:12,621
No?

597
00:52:15,253 --> 00:52:19,838
You teased my younger sister and destroyed our family.

598
00:52:21,424 --> 00:52:23,705
I can't believe you came to our house.

599
00:52:28,920 --> 00:52:34,869
I have cherished her ever since she was a child.

600
00:52:35,150 --> 00:52:39,291
I took her to the bathroom in the middle of the night.

601
00:52:40,383 --> 00:52:45,213
I took care of her every day until she turned 17.

602
00:52:45,954 --> 00:52:48,954
I never had a day where I didn’t see Mon, and I never had a day where I didn’t eat with her.

603
00:52:49,372 --> 00:52:57,017
I have even told her where her mole is.

604
00:52:57,437 --> 00:53:04,517
That’s why I couldn’t forgive her when you got her pregnant.

605
00:53:05,269 --> 00:53:09,974
I tormented Mon—and in the end I treated her like a stray cat or a discarded dog, dirty and discarded.

606
00:53:10,959 --> 00:53:12,295
Everyone hates me.

607
00:53:13,553 --> 00:53:15,376
Everyone took her side.

608
00:53:15,400 --> 00:53:16,529
I thought it was fine.

609
00:53:18,712 --> 00:53:22,803
If I didn't do that, everyone would dislike Mon.

610
00:53:23,583 --> 00:53:26,240
I thought she would lose the will to live.

611
00:53:29,630 --> 00:53:31,826
You’re a student,

612
00:53:31,850 --> 00:53:34,850
You were born a man—so if you just do what you’re meant to do,

613
00:53:35,145 --> 00:53:37,581
You shouldn't have any more business with her.

614
00:53:39,200 --> 00:53:41,616
Hah, it’s something that happens all the time, you know…

615
00:53:41,640 --> 00:53:43,498
If you just throw it away, that’s the end of it

616
00:53:44,259 --> 00:53:46,685
It won't be that easy、That's expecting too much、No such luck

617
00:53:47,492 --> 00:53:50,498
I can’t just give you back cleanly—like that

618
00:53:52,330 --> 00:53:55,068
Did you just come to apologize?

619
00:53:56,340 --> 00:53:59,340
Rather than apologizing, I figured

620
00:53:59,365 --> 00:54:01,474
Do you intend to leave her like that?

621
00:54:02,412 --> 00:54:05,779
If anything comes up, we’ll consult with each other as the two of us

622
00:54:05,979 --> 00:54:07,256
Consult?

623
00:54:08,931 --> 00:54:10,607
You mean you’re going to get married?

624
00:54:10,774 --> 00:54:14,896
If things go that way... maybe

625
00:54:15,710 --> 00:54:17,428
Don't you lie!

626
00:54:19,280 --> 00:54:21,084
Don't be violent towards me.

627
00:54:21,741 --> 00:54:22,741
What?

628
00:54:27,644 --> 00:54:32,107
I know you don't care about anything.

629
00:54:33,310 --> 00:54:36,310
Just think about things like this for once and put up with it!

630
00:54:42,007 --> 00:54:45,794
Mon is no longer the girlfriend she used to be.

631
00:54:45,922 --> 00:54:52,217
Her innocence vanished because of you.

632
00:54:53,829 --> 00:54:56,829
If only you hadn’t even laid a hand on it

633
00:54:56,854 --> 00:54:58,803
Mon wouldn’t become a woman like that anymore.

634
00:55:00,928 --> 00:55:03,319
Don't ever come to my house again.

635
00:55:05,919 --> 00:55:11,326
Promise me you won’t mess with her or anything anymore

636
00:55:12,395 --> 00:55:13,396
I’m sorry.

637
00:55:13,902 --> 00:55:15,646
No matter what you’re told, there’s nothing to be done

638
00:55:16,444 --> 00:55:17,201
I’m sorry.

639
00:55:30,233 --> 00:55:30,842
Go home.

640
00:55:32,826 --> 00:55:33,928
I’m her brother.

641
00:55:35,780 --> 00:55:37,676
If you had a younger sister too,

642
00:55:37,707 --> 00:55:39,451
you should be able to understand what I did

643
00:55:41,381 --> 00:55:42,092
Go home.

644
00:56:13,576 --> 00:56:14,084
Hey.

645
00:56:18,396 --> 00:56:21,834
If you go straight along that embankment and then turn right, the bus stop is there

646
00:56:38,570 --> 00:56:41,584
The date for the wedding was decided without my input.

647
00:56:41,740 --> 00:56:43,232
Did you say clearly, “I don’t want to”?

648
00:56:43,436 --> 00:56:44,006
I did.

649
00:56:44,039 --> 00:56:44,529
Then?

650
00:56:45,784 --> 00:56:50,794
They had no intention of listening to me.

651
00:56:51,279 --> 00:56:53,154
Did you tell them you were going to disappear?

652
00:56:53,733 --> 00:56:59,545
So long as Sanchan is with me, I’m totally fine

653
00:56:59,570 --> 00:57:04,013
No matter what hardships there are, come with me, okay?

654
00:57:07,464 --> 00:57:08,467
It’s so sudden.

655
00:57:09,731 --> 00:57:11,810
Let’s leave here and talk slowly

656
00:57:13,100 --> 00:57:14,646
I’ll be waiting for you at the next Kobashi bus stop

657
00:57:16,554 --> 00:57:17,748
Please come

658
00:57:19,920 --> 00:57:20,803
Kobashi?

659
00:57:25,155 --> 00:57:25,811
I’ll be waiting for you.

660
00:57:33,570 --> 00:57:33,912
Well then

661
00:57:43,881 --> 00:57:44,826
Sorry about that.

662
00:57:47,497 --> 00:57:48,413
How about the customer?

663
00:57:48,561 --> 00:57:49,475
He has left.

664
00:57:51,336 --> 00:57:52,295
What did he come here to do?

665
00:57:52,545 --> 00:57:53,920
He came here to apologize.

666
00:57:55,191 --> 00:57:58,178
Apparently he's really nice. It’s like he went out of his way to come,

667
00:57:58,723 --> 00:58:02,185
He was very apologetic.—so it’s kind of pitiful, honestly

668
00:58:09,130 --> 00:58:12,240
Mom, I have to go home early today, so—

669
00:58:12,419 --> 00:58:14,099
Huh? Why is that?

670
00:58:14,849 --> 00:58:18,029
I just came to say hello and take
a quick look at your face, that’s all

671
00:58:18,579 --> 00:58:20,138
Are you busy at factory?

672
00:58:21,580 --> 00:58:23,276
you said there’s no overtime right now

673
00:58:23,300 --> 00:58:24,123
Because of the economic downturn…

674
00:58:25,121 --> 00:58:27,246
But if an urgent job comes in,

675
00:58:27,270 --> 00:58:28,706
we’re already short on people, too, you know

676
00:58:28,730 --> 00:58:31,404
Hmm, is that so?

677
00:58:32,040 --> 00:58:33,599
But how about at least taking a day off?

678
00:58:34,042 --> 00:58:35,677
I’m thinking of going back on the next bus.

679
00:58:36,039 --> 00:58:36,701
What?

680
00:58:37,990 --> 00:58:40,693
but I shouldn’t get in trouble, though

681
00:58:41,328 --> 00:58:43,373
If I go now, I’ll make it—then

682
00:58:46,084 --> 00:58:49,349
Next time I come, I'll take my time talking with you.

683
00:59:29,116 --> 00:59:29,959
Hurry up.

684
01:00:09,789 --> 01:00:12,789
Anyway, Let's take it easy around Hakone tonight and talk things over.

685
01:00:31,759 --> 01:00:35,318
Boss. I left a fishing net at your house.

686
01:00:39,326 --> 01:00:42,920
The road ahead is full of trucks, so please drive carefully.

687
01:00:43,670 --> 01:00:45,967
Boss.

688
01:00:47,779 --> 01:00:49,396
What's wrong?

689
01:00:50,218 --> 01:00:56,912
I have never been your boss.

690
01:00:58,460 --> 01:01:00,966
I won’t let someone like that be handled by my hands

691
01:01:01,193 --> 01:01:02,396
I get it.

692
01:01:17,879 --> 01:01:19,215
He has become less able to handle alcohol.

693
01:01:56,567 --> 01:01:57,989
Then, let’s go to Atami

694
01:01:58,110 --> 01:01:59,528
We are going to go by Hakone tomorrow

695
01:02:00,138 --> 01:02:01,005
But....

696
01:02:01,372 --> 01:02:03,263
Don't worry about the money.
I brought my card with me for the money

697
01:02:03,288 --> 01:02:04,669
I can take it out anywhere

698
01:02:06,498 --> 01:02:08,943
This is something like a honeymoon.
Hold on.

699
01:03:22,771 --> 01:03:27,872
(I’ll head home so you don’t waste your money—please don’t spend it unnecessarily.)

700
01:04:27,107 --> 01:04:29,317
Hello.

701
01:04:29,342 --> 01:04:30,748
Hello.

702
01:04:45,982 --> 01:04:47,209
Hello.

703
01:05:29,576 --> 01:05:30,482
Old man

704
01:05:31,350 --> 01:05:33,411
May we rent a boat?

705
01:05:37,271 --> 01:05:38,644
This board looks great now that it's been painted.

706
01:05:54,750 --> 01:05:56,950
Oh, sis.

707
01:05:57,349 --> 01:05:59,193
You came from some weird road, didn’t you?

708
01:06:02,318 --> 01:06:03,942
Did we stop by the riverside store?

709
01:06:07,190 --> 01:06:08,161
Was my mom there?

710
01:06:09,340 --> 01:06:10,685
Your dad was asleep.

711
01:06:10,982 --> 01:06:11,943
Really?

712
01:06:12,070 --> 01:06:14,126
Wasn't he minding the shop?

713
01:06:14,150 --> 01:06:15,513
What a lousy dad

714
01:06:16,000 --> 01:06:17,950
But The boats were well-maintained.

715
01:06:18,530 --> 01:06:19,942
Oh, did you see it?

716
01:06:24,154 --> 01:06:24,982
Come on.

717
01:06:25,302 --> 01:06:27,349
Because my mom was complaining

718
01:06:30,585 --> 01:06:34,419
Why is your hairstyle like that?

719
01:06:35,810 --> 01:06:36,568
It's not good.

720
01:06:52,010 --> 01:06:53,544
Say hello.

721
01:06:55,084 --> 01:06:56,123
Hello?

722
01:06:56,852 --> 01:06:58,614
What do you mean 'hello'?

723
01:06:58,799 --> 01:06:59,875
So what are you supposed to say then?

724
01:06:59,900 --> 01:07:00,976
It’s fine if you call me Mom

725
01:07:02,749 --> 01:07:03,835
Go ahead and call

726
01:07:03,947 --> 01:07:04,972
She’ll be surprised

727
01:07:07,825 --> 01:07:08,812
Mom

728
01:07:11,311 --> 01:07:12,224
Mom

729
01:07:12,771 --> 01:07:13,704
Mom

730
01:07:20,785 --> 01:07:22,771
She's always slow

731
01:07:23,192 --> 01:07:24,305
Mom

732
01:07:24,597 --> 01:07:25,317
I'm here.

733
01:07:26,455 --> 01:07:28,788
Hey, come in quickly—you must be getting old

734
01:07:31,418 --> 01:07:33,784
As she grew older, she lost her senses.

735
01:07:36,905 --> 01:07:38,194
Not really.

736
01:07:42,784 --> 01:07:43,897
Hello?

737
01:07:44,946 --> 01:07:49,455
We haven’t seen each other in a while, but

738
01:07:51,200 --> 01:07:52,074
Oh, really?

739
01:07:54,370 --> 01:07:55,622
It’s been a long time

740
01:07:55,910 --> 01:07:57,141
Come on in

741
01:07:57,620 --> 01:08:00,620
I just got my hands dirty a bit, you know

742
01:08:01,290 --> 01:08:04,542
So I thought that for this Bon festival, both of you would come back home

743
01:08:04,950 --> 01:08:07,950
I was getting all fired up since last night, getting everything ready and waiting

744
01:08:08,293 --> 01:08:11,293
San-chan hasn’t been back for quite a while, either

745
01:08:11,573 --> 01:08:15,160
Because, you see, she said she’s going to get some
qualification—an accounting clerk license or something—

746
01:08:15,257 --> 01:08:17,244
and that means she has to
study even on her days off

747
01:08:17,476 --> 01:08:19,475
I thought, well, maybe that’s fine

748
01:08:21,227 --> 01:08:22,047
it’s impressive, really

749
01:08:25,155 --> 01:08:27,539
It’s so hot, isn’t it?

750
01:08:44,692 --> 01:08:45,712
Mom

751
01:08:46,621 --> 01:08:50,237
It looks like a bride came after all like from Marutoyo

752
01:08:50,820 --> 01:08:52,096
I just took a quick look, but...

753
01:08:52,132 --> 01:08:53,601
Hmm, I guess that’s the case

754
01:08:54,140 --> 01:08:56,106
Well, it was already about the time for him to get married

755
01:08:56,164 --> 01:08:58,547
You all come along and try your luck instead of waiting until autumn.

756
01:08:59,850 --> 01:09:01,251
so he really don’t hold back, huh

757
01:09:01,619 --> 01:09:04,055
His wife’s just full of excuses

758
01:09:04,370 --> 01:09:06,350
Tokiko Grandma also came wearing two layers Kimono

759
01:09:06,723 --> 01:09:09,922
Well, underneath the obi belt gets all sweaty, and when she goes into the bath,

760
01:09:10,029 --> 01:09:12,175
it’s like she gave it up for a whole month

761
01:09:14,455 --> 01:09:17,333
Huh, so even boring stories can come through, As usual,

762
01:09:18,939 --> 01:09:21,510
uh, the other day, um...

763
01:09:23,325 --> 01:09:25,577
Oh, that person—Obata-san—he came by

764
01:09:26,349 --> 01:09:26,644
Huh?

765
01:09:27,337 --> 01:09:28,770
Obata-san

766
01:09:29,574 --> 01:09:30,361
When?

767
01:09:32,543 --> 01:09:34,157
I wonder why he came

768
01:09:34,516 --> 01:09:36,548
Huh, so this is his address

769
01:09:41,877 --> 01:09:43,388
It was 3 months ago.

770
01:09:44,147 --> 01:09:46,860
So it was a wig, huh?

771
01:09:47,210 --> 01:09:48,826
He came by and visit us out of the blue

772
01:09:48,851 --> 01:09:49,589
I wonder why.

773
01:09:50,073 --> 01:09:51,826
he showed up and said he
would come up with an apology

774
01:09:53,173 --> 01:09:54,291
He met Dad?

775
01:09:54,527 --> 01:09:54,840
Yes.

776
01:09:55,414 --> 01:09:56,334
What he said?

777
01:09:56,779 --> 01:10:00,039
Dad?, not really—anyway

778
01:10:00,711 --> 01:10:01,645
Did he talk calm?

779
01:10:01,897 --> 01:10:06,550
Yeah, he’s pretty calm—and it’s quite rare for him,

780
01:10:06,690 --> 01:10:09,083
Mr. Obata, Mr.Obata—like, using the polite form, I mean

781
01:10:09,350 --> 01:10:12,690
I was very worried, thinking he would get angry.

782
01:10:12,796 --> 01:10:16,073
but he’s actually fairly gentlemanly
and talked to him gently

783
01:10:17,545 --> 01:10:19,893
I see.
I was sorry.

784
01:10:21,132 --> 01:10:23,292
He didn't need to come here.

785
01:10:24,135 --> 01:10:25,428
Didn’t you meet with my brother?

786
01:10:25,728 --> 01:10:27,147
I didn’t meet with your older brother.

787
01:10:28,053 --> 01:10:28,725
I see.

788
01:10:29,724 --> 01:10:32,312
Whenever he gets involved, there really ends up being trouble.

789
01:10:32,751 --> 01:10:35,284
Fortunately, he was not here.

790
01:10:36,441 --> 01:10:37,128
You know what?

791
01:10:39,880 --> 01:10:42,880
He was really cool, wasn't he?

792
01:10:43,272 --> 01:10:43,850
What?

793
01:10:45,107 --> 01:10:46,123
That person.

794
01:10:46,685 --> 01:10:48,068
You are stupid.

795
01:10:48,353 --> 01:10:52,045
He got you pregnant, you shouldn't be praising him.

796
01:10:52,070 --> 01:10:53,385
I am absolutely fed up.

797
01:10:55,363 --> 01:10:56,206
Mom

798
01:10:57,432 --> 01:10:58,609
Another souvenir?

799
01:10:58,980 --> 01:11:01,276
Sorry about that

800
01:11:01,700 --> 01:11:04,700
My souvenir is there, too.

801
01:11:06,238 --> 01:11:06,893
This?

802
01:11:08,562 --> 01:11:10,000
This is a yukata.

803
01:11:10,513 --> 01:11:12,479
There are 3 of them.

804
01:11:12,605 --> 01:11:13,683
Two of them are for men.

805
01:11:13,917 --> 01:11:15,706
So for dad and Ino?

806
01:11:17,487 --> 01:11:19,128
That is yours.

807
01:11:20,016 --> 01:11:20,899
This?

808
01:11:21,964 --> 01:11:23,972
I thought clothes would be a good choice for you.

809
01:11:24,636 --> 01:11:26,417
This is see-through, isn't it?

810
01:11:28,979 --> 01:11:32,417
You didn't have to buy something so expensive like this.

811
01:11:33,175 --> 01:11:34,964
Is this mine?

812
01:11:38,983 --> 01:11:42,865
This is a really classy pattern of your own, isn’t it?

813
01:11:43,917 --> 01:11:46,475
Look—this isn’t just an ordinary yukata

814
01:11:46,500 --> 01:11:48,175
It says ‘Koubai yukata’ on it

815
01:11:48,641 --> 01:11:51,073
This is for special occasion.

816
01:11:51,167 --> 01:11:53,308
This is lightweight and of very high quality.

817
01:11:53,400 --> 01:11:55,659
Only people from upper-class families own this.

818
01:11:57,456 --> 01:11:59,151
I forgot to pour the tea.

819
01:11:59,176 --> 01:12:00,392
I drink water, so I don't need that.

820
01:12:00,900 --> 01:12:03,721
The water from our well is very delicious.

821
01:12:03,858 --> 01:12:07,064
You see, the water doesn’t come out anymore Lately

822
01:12:07,238 --> 01:12:12,016
They’ve dug a big new well for the air conditioning, and The well has stopped producing water.

823
01:12:12,041 --> 01:12:17,532
I swear it's true—every day they keep building
concrete companies, big dormitories, and apartments.

824
01:12:21,644 --> 01:12:23,792
Your water alone will suffice.

825
01:12:25,256 --> 01:12:26,581
Yeah

826
01:12:30,035 --> 01:12:30,910
Sis.

827
01:12:33,800 --> 01:12:36,800
What was so great about this person named Obata?

828
01:12:38,099 --> 01:12:41,217
I’m sure there are even better people out there in the world.

829
01:12:41,242 --> 01:12:43,389
Sure, there probably are.

830
01:12:47,980 --> 01:12:48,993
The world is a big place

831
01:12:50,159 --> 01:12:56,185
Sure, there were some who were even more handsome—maybe they were starving, or maybe they were generous—

832
01:12:56,210 --> 01:12:58,118
but some were rough and scratchy and all that

833
01:12:58,576 --> 01:13:02,840
You know, he was only that person who was just right

834
01:13:04,267 --> 01:13:06,107
Men are dirty.

835
01:13:06,590 --> 01:13:08,386
If it’s only like me, I’ll do the kind of thing where I make men happy from my side

836
01:13:08,410 --> 01:13:10,957
—something I can do, so that I can laugh at what’s going on inside her—though

837
01:13:11,549 --> 01:13:13,685
Men taught that to me

838
01:13:16,246 --> 01:13:17,328
I don’t know what made me think

839
01:13:17,360 --> 01:13:19,492
this time it’s the real thing, but...

840
01:13:19,990 --> 01:13:21,238
They are all the same

841
01:13:23,228 --> 01:13:25,295
Do you date a guy?

842
01:13:27,059 --> 01:13:27,779
Why?

843
01:13:28,233 --> 01:13:29,060
You want?

844
01:13:30,293 --> 01:13:32,840
I can’t just be thinking about men like that all the time

845
01:13:33,812 --> 01:13:35,205
I’ve got to study too

846
01:13:35,916 --> 01:13:37,715
Marriage isn’t the purpose of my life.

847
01:13:40,468 --> 01:13:42,035
The important thing is living, right?

848
01:13:42,070 --> 01:13:43,432
It sounds pretty serious, doesn’t it?

849
01:13:44,430 --> 01:13:48,555
So if that person named Obata-End comes by right now, What will you do?

850
01:13:49,286 --> 01:13:51,240
I won’t be able to be together with him

851
01:13:51,910 --> 01:13:54,440
I only like him when I’m thinking about him.

852
01:13:55,416 --> 01:13:57,740
He's become lukewarm toward me, too.

853
01:13:59,513 --> 01:14:00,837
You wouldn’t understand, San-chan

854
01:14:19,303 --> 01:14:20,163
Ino!

855
01:14:21,486 --> 01:14:25,768
You work hard.
Hey, is your dad doing well?

856
01:14:25,967 --> 01:14:29,062
Ah, what a shame. You’re still like a monk

857
01:14:29,498 --> 01:14:30,438
well then,

858
01:14:32,010 --> 01:14:33,070
Keep going and earn money.

859
01:14:33,392 --> 01:14:35,665
Ah, you too—quickly, you rush in making money.

860
01:14:36,838 --> 01:14:37,855
Oh my god.

861
01:14:45,095 --> 01:14:46,675
Shall we have a lunch together.

862
01:14:47,949 --> 01:14:48,921
Oi, ugh, it’s so hot.

863
01:14:50,820 --> 01:14:51,927
Leader.

864
01:14:52,772 --> 01:14:56,774
I can’t be motivated without tips—please, I’m counting on you

865
01:14:57,130 --> 01:14:59,309
What? Again?

866
01:15:04,373 --> 01:15:06,083
She really fell asleep

867
01:15:06,410 --> 01:15:09,410
Just leave her alone—she’ll cool off soon

868
01:15:11,736 --> 01:15:13,376
She was so upset

869
01:15:14,494 --> 01:15:16,188
She didn’t get enough sleep or rest

870
01:15:19,278 --> 01:15:20,396
Thank you.

871
01:15:21,519 --> 01:15:23,378
You too—take care, okay?

872
01:15:23,824 --> 01:15:24,404
For what?

873
01:15:25,528 --> 01:15:27,992
Because someone said that at the station saw you

874
01:15:28,360 --> 01:15:29,764
Well, you know

875
01:15:29,871 --> 01:15:31,624
It will be fine.

876
01:15:32,410 --> 01:15:34,230
They’ve taken a wife.

877
01:15:34,820 --> 01:15:36,405
That adopted child turned out to be just fine after all

878
01:15:37,223 --> 01:15:40,906
I thought he’d be a little braver, though

879
01:15:41,320 --> 01:15:43,236
Oh—if he put me up to being brave,

880
01:15:43,261 --> 01:15:46,261
it’ll be the exact same nightmare as what happened before

881
01:15:47,773 --> 01:15:48,938
So were you thrown out?

882
01:15:49,396 --> 01:15:51,225
Are you awake?

883
01:15:51,900 --> 01:15:54,149
I’m going to find a good man for you.

884
01:15:55,340 --> 01:15:57,186
That guy called Okan—or whatever

885
01:15:57,217 --> 01:15:59,589
On the way back, you know, he just bit a manju in the bus

886
01:16:00,162 --> 01:16:00,895
Did you see?

887
01:16:01,600 --> 01:16:03,825
Yeah, he's kind of like a kid

888
01:16:03,934 --> 01:16:04,821
But I hate it.

889
01:16:05,073 --> 01:16:06,993
There’s something cute about him

890
01:16:07,370 --> 01:16:08,711
He look so calm and easygoing.

891
01:16:09,796 --> 01:16:11,507
He can't keep fretting about it for all that time

892
01:16:11,532 --> 01:16:13,162
He's not going to keep taking the blame

893
01:16:13,430 --> 01:16:14,173
Mom

894
01:16:14,920 --> 01:16:15,740
I'm starving.

895
01:16:18,568 --> 01:16:19,178
Hey.

896
01:16:20,052 --> 01:16:22,459
That disgrace of a woman has come back home again.

897
01:16:24,180 --> 01:16:26,005
You’re working even today, huh?

898
01:16:26,052 --> 01:16:27,802
I guess he's just doing this as a temporary helper

899
01:16:28,005 --> 01:16:28,858
pretty interesting, huh?

900
01:16:29,091 --> 01:16:31,137
Even though everyone else has gone back to their home country...

901
01:16:31,170 --> 01:16:33,201
For me, there is no Obon or New Year's.

902
01:16:34,628 --> 01:16:37,628
He spent all his time playing, so he is very busy now.

903
01:16:43,131 --> 01:16:46,052
You probably plans to go on eating for about a week too

904
01:16:46,861 --> 01:16:50,060
I really wish you’d get out of here already—quickly

905
01:16:50,790 --> 01:16:52,974
This is a private home.

906
01:16:53,403 --> 01:16:56,536
During lunch, you can have ankoro and takuan here

907
01:16:56,799 --> 01:16:58,193
I’ll treat you to a meal again

908
01:16:58,819 --> 01:17:04,709
No matter what you do for her, she won't get any better.

909
01:17:05,114 --> 01:17:06,310
Cut it out.

910
01:17:06,638 --> 01:17:08,654
It's been a while, and my sister finally came by, you know?

911
01:17:08,780 --> 01:17:11,780
You'll end up acting like a fool if you get involved with her.

912
01:17:12,389 --> 01:17:15,873
Look—what a great pattern, for a souvenir

913
01:17:15,898 --> 01:17:17,670
Mon bought it for me.

914
01:17:18,204 --> 01:17:20,912
I’ll buy as many rolls as you want

915
01:17:20,983 --> 01:17:22,639
This is for you.

916
01:17:25,669 --> 01:17:30,209
Don’t insult me. I’m not going to come running happily with my
hands out. just because you bought it for me with dirty money

917
01:17:30,685 --> 01:17:34,005
While you don’t have a proper job,

918
01:17:34,030 --> 01:17:35,686
I don’t want you coming around here

919
01:17:35,771 --> 01:17:38,326
Alright, be quiet now—come on, everyone, let’s eat

920
01:17:39,084 --> 01:17:40,302
Hey, sis, you too—let’s eat

921
01:17:40,454 --> 01:17:43,474
Come over here, okay? It’s the break time

922
01:17:44,833 --> 01:17:46,615
We’re about to go to a CM.

923
01:17:47,381 --> 01:17:49,556
Let’s call the fight off—okay?

924
01:18:08,068 --> 01:18:08,869
Tea

925
01:18:09,834 --> 01:18:11,037
Do you want to eat ochazuke?

926
01:18:12,598 --> 01:18:14,559
It’s all over, anyway

927
01:18:14,873 --> 01:18:19,545
What do you mean?
The man who came the other day shouldn't have come here either.

928
01:18:20,652 --> 01:18:25,177
He came here because you are being looked down upon.

929
01:18:27,773 --> 01:18:30,115
You met him?

930
01:18:30,420 --> 01:18:31,506
What happened if I met him?

931
01:18:32,318 --> 01:18:33,021
Where?

932
01:18:33,983 --> 01:18:35,154
I followed him.

933
01:18:35,277 --> 01:18:36,373
He was on his way home.

934
01:18:36,398 --> 01:18:37,466
What did you do?

935
01:18:39,858 --> 01:18:40,803
What did you do?

936
01:18:43,022 --> 01:18:43,701
What did you do?

937
01:18:43,726 --> 01:18:45,029
I knocked him out.

938
01:18:47,040 --> 01:18:50,040
He did not attack me.

939
01:18:50,380 --> 01:18:52,316
My chest felt so light—like a breeze

940
01:18:52,340 --> 01:18:55,950
Hey! Say it again—what did you just say?

941
01:18:56,540 --> 01:18:57,816
What happened to that guy?

942
01:18:57,840 --> 01:18:59,442
I should’ve killed him halfway,

943
01:19:01,099 --> 01:19:02,513
You bastard!

944
01:19:03,053 --> 01:19:05,154
You didn't need to use violence against him.

945
01:19:05,474 --> 01:19:07,105
You have nothing with him

946
01:19:07,130 --> 01:19:08,715
Why do you have to be so rough?

947
01:19:08,740 --> 01:19:09,521
Mon

948
01:19:09,546 --> 01:19:10,162
Sis.

949
01:19:10,693 --> 01:19:11,420
What?

950
01:19:12,350 --> 01:19:14,052
who are you talking to?
You bastard!

951
01:19:14,077 --> 01:19:15,497
This is my body!

952
01:19:16,216 --> 01:19:19,693
Why are you making a big fuss when I did it to him on my own?

953
01:19:20,585 --> 01:19:22,810
Why did you go and half-kill him?!

954
01:19:23,280 --> 01:19:24,440
Stop it! Please!

955
01:19:24,465 --> 01:19:27,815
Why are you hitting and kicking someone
who’s not even lifting a finger?

956
01:19:27,840 --> 01:19:28,941
Shut up!

957
01:19:35,464 --> 01:19:36,183
You're a coward.

958
01:19:40,105 --> 01:19:40,659
Stop!

959
01:19:45,548 --> 01:19:47,084
You bastard!

960
01:19:49,009 --> 01:19:50,784
You bastard!

961
01:19:50,988 --> 01:19:52,034
Stop!

962
01:19:56,449 --> 01:19:58,729
Please! Bro! Bro! Bro—stop it!

963
01:20:00,511 --> 01:20:03,074
Have you still not woken up?
You bastard!

964
01:20:05,610 --> 01:20:06,300
Stop!

965
01:20:10,495 --> 01:20:11,917
He is an important person to me.

966
01:20:11,942 --> 01:20:13,316
Stop it, Ino.

967
01:20:13,347 --> 01:20:14,402
Stop it

968
01:20:15,741 --> 01:20:16,517
Stop it

969
01:20:16,558 --> 01:20:18,995
You are nothing but a prostitute.

970
01:20:19,658 --> 01:20:20,909
Bro! Stop it.

971
01:20:21,222 --> 01:20:21,964
Slap me.

972
01:20:23,925 --> 01:20:27,378
Slap me if you want.

973
01:20:27,753 --> 01:20:28,339
Slap me.

974
01:20:30,172 --> 01:20:35,784
You're a country bumpkin—a foolish man living off a woman's money.

975
01:20:37,027 --> 01:20:42,402
You are not my older brother.

976
01:20:42,427 --> 01:20:45,027
You should be mindful of your language and speak in a ladylike manner.

977
01:20:45,052 --> 01:20:47,706
Kill me if you want.

978
01:20:47,925 --> 01:20:48,737
I will.

979
01:20:48,762 --> 01:20:49,956
Bro! Stop it.

980
01:20:50,136 --> 01:20:51,339
Cut it out

981
01:20:51,722 --> 01:20:54,527
Both of you are at fault.

982
01:21:00,706 --> 01:21:05,252
Get out of here already.

983
01:21:27,332 --> 01:21:31,575
You’ve really become quite a woman, huh

984
01:21:33,350 --> 01:21:35,167
Not really, Mom

985
01:21:36,310 --> 01:21:38,310
You don't have to worry so much.

986
01:21:40,474 --> 01:21:42,824
Because you're the first woman I've ever known who could say things like that

987
01:21:44,430 --> 01:21:46,042
Please, I’m begging you

988
01:21:46,360 --> 01:21:50,651
Be serious and get more feminine

989
01:21:52,081 --> 01:21:55,448
because if you carry on like that, you’re no
different from being more than your brother

990
01:21:59,537 --> 01:22:04,381
But I won’t become as awful a woman as my mom thinks I will

991
01:22:05,260 --> 01:22:07,693
But it’s already no good

992
01:22:23,070 --> 01:22:25,287
I don’t need stuff like this anymore!

993
01:22:47,120 --> 01:22:48,740
Anyway, I'm going.

994
01:22:49,303 --> 01:22:50,264
Did you bring incense sticks?

995
01:22:51,537 --> 01:22:54,385
I’ll go offer some to Jizo Statue for Unborn Children too

996
01:22:54,410 --> 01:22:56,627
That is a Jizo statue for babies?

997
01:22:57,920 --> 01:22:59,988
Don’t drink too much

998
01:23:00,401 --> 01:23:02,340
The change for the alcohol is over there—just leave it there

999
01:24:02,454 --> 01:24:04,531
At night, everything looks beautiful, doesn’t it?

1000
01:24:05,660 --> 01:24:06,839
It’s romantic, you know

1001
01:24:08,726 --> 01:24:09,994
Even if Ino brother is ugly,

1002
01:24:11,964 --> 01:24:12,839
It could be.

1003
01:24:44,830 --> 01:24:46,450
We'll walk on that bridge?

1004
01:24:47,138 --> 01:24:48,611
It's hot, isn't it?

1005
01:24:49,472 --> 01:24:51,382
I probably can't come by for a while, though

1006
01:24:53,060 --> 01:24:54,578
When will you come again, Sis?

1007
01:24:56,320 --> 01:24:58,658
Whenever I ever feel like seeing Mom and others.

1008
01:25:00,599 --> 01:25:03,479
Even a brother like that—so awful—I sometimes still feel like seeing his face.

1009
01:25:11,518 --> 01:25:12,119
Old man.

1010
01:26:08,876 --> 01:26:10,754
Bitches!
Where are you going?

1011
01:26:11,355 --> 01:26:12,262
A bus stop.

1012
01:26:12,438 --> 01:26:13,658
Don't call us bitches.

1013
01:26:14,721 --> 01:26:16,275
Where are you going by bus, Bitches?

1014
01:26:16,801 --> 01:26:17,668
A station.

1015
01:26:18,659 --> 01:26:20,799
I mean,Where are you going by train?

1016
01:26:21,539 --> 01:26:22,599
To Tokyo.

1017
01:26:22,792 --> 01:26:23,881
Where in Tokyo?

1018
01:26:24,366 --> 01:26:25,246
Our office.

1019
01:26:26,223 --> 01:26:27,012
How about you?

1020
01:26:30,208 --> 01:26:31,208
Get in the car.

1021
01:26:33,340 --> 01:26:34,557
I guess we'll just have to get in the car for his sake.

1022
01:26:57,484 --> 01:26:59,292
It's okay to drop us off along the way.

1023
01:27:11,694 --> 01:27:14,167
Come back home again.

1024
01:27:17,565 --> 01:27:18,890
Mon, Promise me.

1025
01:27:21,706 --> 01:27:24,745
Don't go far away from me, okay?

1026
01:28:14,838 --> 01:28:21,487
THE END

